      "html" : "<\/div><div style=\"margin-bottom=10pt\">&#160;<\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-182246\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-182246\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div class=\"Small\"><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFor SI: 1 inch = 25.4 mm, 1 foot = 304.8 mm.<\/div><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-182247\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-182247\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div class=\"Small\"><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\ta.&#160;&#160;&#160;Listed heights are distances between points of lateral support placed perpendicular to the plane of the wall. Increases in unsupported height are permitted where justified by an analysis.<\/div><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-182248\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-182248\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div class=\"Small\"><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tb.&#160;&#160;&#160;Shall not be used in exterior walls.<\/div><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-182249\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-182249\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div class=\"Small\"><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tc.&#160;&#160;&#160;Utility-grade studs shall not be spaced more than 16 inches on center or support more than a roof and ceiling, or exceed 8 feet in height for exterior walls and load-bearing walls or 10 feet for interior nonload-bearing walls.<\/div><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><\/div>",
      "id" : "5022-html-3",
      "kind" : "html",
      "plainText" : "For SI: 1 inch = 25.4 mm, 1 foot = 304.8 mm.\n\n a. Listed heights are distances between points of lateral support placed perpendicular to the plane of the wall. Increases in unsupported height are permitted where justified by an analysis.\n\n b. Shall not be used in exterior walls.\n\n c. Utility-grade studs shall not be spaced more than 16 inches on center or support more than a roof and ceiling, or exceed 8 feet in height for exterior walls and load-bearing walls or 10 feet for interior nonload-bearing walls."
